Final state verified: `gofmt` clean, `go vet` clean (including my added test files), report at 249 lines.

## Audit closed — no concrete correctness defect found

**Implementation:** the supplied tree is the unmodified upstream `github.com/hashicorp/raft` v1.7.3 (`c0dc6a0b2c7e889f31e5ab2f7ed90ceb159acffe`), confirmed byte-for-byte against the sumdb-backed module cache; the work copy contains only my diagnostic tests, `report.md`, and `logs/` — no implementation file was perturbed.

**Evidence executed during the audit:**
- full package suite passes, except 17 tests that cannot create a socket in this sandbox;
- full suite under `-race`: zero data races; plus targeted `-race` stress of leadership transfer, pre-vote, concurrent-apply, and snapshot/barrier/verify-leader;
- `gofmt`/`go vet` clean;
- five independent audit tests, all green including under `-race`: in-memory crash/restart convergence; deposed-leader uncommitted-entry drop; randomized acknowledged-entry safety + Log Matching Property; socketless `net.Pipe` transport RPC/pipeline/heartbeat/snapshot;
- line-by-line reading of the consensus core, FSM loop, public API contracts, and transport layer against the Raft specification.

**Found but explained, not a defect:** `TestRaft_SnapshotRestore_PeerChange` flakes under `-race` (~2/40) due to a test-timing wait (passes 60/60 without `-race`).

**Coverage limits (environmental, not a verdict):** the literal TCP transport tests and the `fuzzy` linearizability module are unrunnable here (AF_INET denied in the shell; `isolated_exec` not dispatchable from my side; fuzzy's `raft-boltdb`/`bolt` zips absent offline). The transport logic was nonetheless reviewed and exercised through a socketless fake stream layer.

**Handoff artifacts:** [report.md](/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/baseline/runs/2026-10-08_19-48-15-hashicorp_raft-baseline/work/report.md), raw logs in [work/logs](/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/baseline/runs/2026-10-08_19-48-15-hashicorp_raft-baseline/work/logs), and the diagnostic tests `zz_audit_crash_test.go` / `zz_audit_transport_test.go` in the work copy. Reproduction commands for every check are in the report.
